<header class="ref-head"><span class="hero-ornament"></span><h1 class="research-title">22 February in history</h1><p class="ref-lede">9 events that happened on 22 February, from 896 to 1997.</p></header>
<ol class="day-events"><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/896">896 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">1,130 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Pope Formosus crowns Arnulf of Carinthia emperor in Rome</h2><p class="tih-event-desc"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/arnulf-of-carinthia">Arnulf of Carinthia</a>, king of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/east-francia">East Francia</a>, invaded <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/italy">Italy</a> again and was crowned emperor in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rome">Rome</a> by Pope Formosus, but soon went back to East <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/francia">Francia</a>. Formosus's remains were later exhumed and tried in the Cadaver Synod for siding with Arnulf.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/arnulf-of-carinthia">Arnulf of Carinthia</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/imperator-romanorum">Imperator Romanorum</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb tih-event-hero"><p class="tih-hero-kicker">&#10022; Anniversary of the day</p><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/pope-gregory-vii" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/pope-gregory-vii.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1076">1076 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">950 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Pope Gregory VII excommunicates Henry IV</h2><p class="tih-event-desc"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pope-gregory-vii">Pope Gregory VII</a> pronounced a sentence of excommunication against Henry IV, king of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/germany">Germany</a>, stripped him of his royal dignity and released his subjects from their oaths of allegiance. Their struggle led to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/prince-henry-the-navigator">Henry</a>'s penance at Canossa in 1077.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pope-gregory-vii">Pope Gregory VII</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/henry-iv-holy-roman-emperor">Henry IV, Holy Roman Emperor</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1288">1288 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">738 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">The Franciscan Girolamo Maschi is elected Pope Nicholas IV</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Girolamo Maschi, a Franciscan, was elected pope and took the name Nicholas IV, the first Franciscan to hold the office. He reigned until his death on 4 April 1292.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/franciscans">Franciscans</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1495">1495 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">531 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Charles VIII of France enters Naples</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">After a rapid march through <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/italy">Italy</a>, the French king took <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/naples">Naples</a> almost without a fight. A coalition of Italian states, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/spain">Spain</a> and the Emperor soon forced him out, but the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/italian-wars">Italian Wars</a> had begun.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag tih-tag-profile" href="/empire/kingdom-of-naples">Kingdom of Naples</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/italian-wars">Italian Wars</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1732">1732 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">294 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">George Washington is born in Virginia</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Born at Popes <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/muscogee">Creek</a> in Westmoreland County, Washington commanded the Continental Army in the Revolutionary War and became the first President of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/united-states">United States</a>.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/united-states">United States</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/virginia">Virginia</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1819">1819 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">207 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Spain cedes Florida in the Adams-Onís Treaty</h2><p class="tih-event-desc"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/spain">Spain</a> gave <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/florida">Florida</a> to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/united-states">United States</a> and agreed a boundary running to the Pacific. In return the US assumed claims of its citizens against Spain and gave up its claim to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/texas">Texas</a>.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/united-states">United States</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1847">1847 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">179 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Battle of Buena Vista begins in northern Mexico</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Zachary Taylor's outnumbered army held off Santa Anna's attacks over two days near Saltillo. Santa Anna withdrew, and Taylor's fame carried him to the presidency in 1848.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mexico">Mexico</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1980">1980 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">46 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">US amateurs beat the Soviet Union in the 'Miracle on Ice'</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">A team of American college players defeated the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/soviet-union">Soviet Union</a>, four-time Olympic champions, 4-3 at the Lake Placid Winter Olympics. The US went on to win the gold medal.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/soviet-union">Soviet Union</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1997">1997 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">29 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Scientists announce Dolly the sheep, the first clone of an adult mammal</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Researchers at the Roslin Institute near <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/edinburgh">Edinburgh</a> revealed they had cloned a sheep from an adult cell. Dolly, born in July 1996, sparked worldwide debate on the ethics of cloning.</p></div></li></ol>
<section class="day-ppl" aria-labelledby="day-born"><h2 class="ref-sec-title" id="day-born">Born on 22 February <span class="n">5</span></h2><ul class="enc-seealso"><li><a href="/encyclopedia/charles-vii-of-france"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/charles-vii-of-france.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Charles VII of France</span><span class="tp">1403–1461</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/tahmasp-i"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/tahmasp-i.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Tahmasp I</span><span class="tp">1514–1576</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/george-washington"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/george-washington.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">George Washington</span><span class="tp">1732–1799</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/victor-raul-haya-de-la-torre"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/victor-raul-haya-de-la-torre.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Víctor Raúl Haya de la Torre</span><span class="tp">1895–1979</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/romulo-betancourt"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/romulo-betancourt.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Rómulo Betancourt</span><span class="tp">1908–1981</span></span></a></li></ul></section>
<section class="day-ppl" aria-labelledby="day-died"><h2 class="ref-sec-title" id="day-died">Died on 22 February <span class="n">8</span></h2><ul class="enc-seealso"><li><a href="/encyclopedia/guo-wei"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/guo-wei.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Guo Wei</span><span class="tp">904–954</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/garcia-sanchez-i-of-pamplona"><span class="ph ph-person" aria-hidden="true"></span><span><span class="nm">García Sánchez I of Pamplona</span><span class="tp">c. 919–970</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/arnulf-iii-count-of-flanders"><span class="ph ph-person" aria-hidden="true"></span><span><span class="nm">Arnulf III, Count of Flanders</span><span class="tp">c. 1055–1071</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/roger-borsa"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/roger-borsa.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Roger Borsa</span><span class="tp">c. 1060–1111</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/david-ii-of-scotland"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/david-ii-of-scotland.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">David II of Scotland</span><span class="tp">1324–1371</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/adam-ferguson"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/adam-ferguson.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Adam Ferguson</span><span class="tp">1723–1816</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/heungseon-daewongun"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/heungseon-daewongun.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Heungseon Daewongun</span><span class="tp">1820–1898</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/francisco-i-madero"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/francisco-i-madero.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Francisco I. Madero</span><span class="tp">1873–1913</span></span></a></li></ul></section>
<p class="day-ppl-note">Dates as the sources give them: in the Julian calendar before 1582, and in some countries for longer (Britain until 1752, Russia until 1918). Only people whose day of birth or death the records agree on are listed.</p>
